/*
Acsent of men

4 phases mineral, plant, animal, human
1..4 dimentions: pitch, volume, articulation, timbre

Phase one has one dimention phase two 2 etc

13: 0..12 semitones the highest is the target, triangular weighted random with low emphasis.

Initially only the lowest note is played, on hitting the target the ambitus is increased by one.

Random value from that ambities range is played on each attempt

When the range is full the phase is finished.

Duration factor ( fixed duration/highest amplitude value) is taken from the current amplitude range (1..n) mapped to become gradually smaller.

Higher phases have random values from the current ambitus for the extra dimention

In general from long to short

*/

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ascent -- what the comment above asks for, as words.
//
// Hear it:    "mus/ascent.mus" load   '[2] start         the phases in the list, one after another:
//             '[1] start (the mineral)  '[1 2 3 4] start (all four, computing them takes some
//             seconds first)  '[2 4] start (the plant, then the human)
// Change it:  7 :seed T!   (another run)    '[1 1 1 1] :unit T!  (a list, a value for each phase)   '[...] :ladder T!   then start
//             '[1 3 1 1] :voices T!   voices per phase: a canon, each voice the same notes
//             '[2 2 2 2] :delay T!   units between one voice's entry and the next's (:unit each)
// Stop it:    stop
//
// A phase climbs an ambitus of 13 semitones (0..:top, 12). The ambitus starts as the lowest note
// alone. Each attempt draws a note from it, a triangular draw weighted to the low end, so the
// highest note, the target, is rare. When it is hit the ambitus grows by one, and the new
// highest note is the target. When the ambitus is full and its top is hit, the phase is
// finished. A note lasts the fixed duration (:unit) divided by the number of values of the
// ambitus there are now (the highest amplitude value): long to short. Phase 1 (mineral) has
// pitch only; phase 2 (plant) adds volume, 3 (animal) articulation, 4 (human) timbre, each
// drawn from the ambitus at that moment and mapped on its scale, so it widens as the
// ambitus does. The dimensions a phase does not have yet are fixed.

'numeric.random 'r reqalgo            // r/int-lo-emph r/int-range
'numeric.rng 'rng reqalgo             // rng/seed

// ---- the settings ------------------------------------------------------------

// A setting that is a list has a value for each phase, the first for phase 1 (mineral), the
// last for phase 4 (human), as :fixedtimbres has.
'[3 2 3 7/2] :unit T!                                // the fixed duration, in whole notes: the first note, a breve
'[4 4 2 3/2] :delay T!                               // in units: how much later each voice of a canon enters than the one before (4 units of 2 whole notes: 8)
'[24 36 48 72] :base T!                            // the lowest note, C2: the ambitus an octave above it
'[12 12 12 12] :top T!                             // the highest semitone above it: 13 notes in all
'[70 70 70 70] :loudness T!                        // the volume a phase has before its volume is a dimension
'[ '[32 70 60] '[40] 68] :fixedtimbres T!       // the fixed timbre of phase 1, 2, 3; a list is layered: bassoon and acoustic bass together, then flute, oboe
// the timbre ladder, the value 0..:top of the human phase: from mineral to human, each rung
// two or three programs sounding together (multitimbral), chosen for the low register --
// timpani and marimba, marimba and piano, piano and church organ, organ and acoustic bass,
// bass and bassoon, bassoon and clarinet, clarinet and baritone sax, baritone sax and trombone,
// trombone and tuba, tuba and horn, horn and contrabass, contrabass, cello and choir aahs,
// cello, choir aahs and voice oohs
'[ '[47 12] '[12 0] '[0 19] '[19 32] '[32 70] '[70 71] '[71 67] '[67 57] '[57 58] '[58 60] '[60 43] '[43 42 52] '[42 52 53] ] :ladder T!
// the articulation ladder: short to long
'[:staccatissimo :staccato :staccato :portato :portato :portato :tenuto :tenuto :tenuto :legato :legato :legato :legato] :artics T!
5 :seed T!                                         // the draws: the same seed, the same run
120 :tempo T!                                      // quarter notes a minute
'[1 2 3 4] :voices T!                              // voices of each phase: the same phase as a canon, each voice the same notes

// ---- one level of a phase: the attempts at a target --------------------------

// the draws at the target n: notes of the ambitus 0..n, low ones the likeliest, up to and
// including the first time the target is hit
: attempts ( $n -- draws )
  //'( 0 $n 1 + r/int-lo-emph )  $n 1 + dup * 12 *  pull        // more than it needs, on average ten times
  '( 0 $n 1 + r/rand-int )  $n 1 + dup * 12 *  pull        // more than it needs, on average ten times
  '[1] $n *  concat                                            // and the target at the end, should it not be hit
  dup $n index-of 1 +  take
  $n 0 >  '( '[1] $n *  swap concat )  '( )  if ;                // the target just allowed is played first

// count values of the ambitus 0..n, each as likely as another: what an extra dimension draws
: extras ( $n $count -- values ) '( 0 $n 1 + r/int-range ) $count pull ;

// the value of a setting for a phase: the setting is a list, a value for each phase
: per-phase ( $key $phase -- value ) $key T@@ $phase 1 - @ ;

// the columns of a level (arithmetic on whole lists: a list and a number)
: durations-of ( $n $p $phase -- list )
  $p 0 *  :unit $phase per-phase $n 1 + /  +      // the unit over the values there are
  $n :top $phase per-phase =                      // the last level: its last note, the top hit, is as long as the first
  '( dup length 1 - take  '[1] :unit $phase per-phase *  concat )  '( )  if ;
: pitches-of ( $p $phase -- list ) $p :base $phase per-phase + ;
: volumes-of ( $a $phase -- list ) $a 75.0 * :top $phase per-phase / 25 + ;            // 0..:top on 25..100
: articulations-of ( $a -- list ) $a '( :artics T@@ swap @ ) map ;
: timbres-of ( $a -- list ) $a '( :ladder T@@ swap @ ) map ;

// a level of phase p: the notes of its attempts at the target n, the dimensions the phase has
: level-of ( $n $phase $p -- seq )
  | $n $p $phase durations-of  $p $phase pitches-of
    :volume
      $phase 2 >=  '( $n $p length extras $phase volumes-of )  '( ( :loudness $phase per-phase ) )  if
    :articulation
      $phase 3 >=  '( $n $p length extras articulations-of )  '( '[:portato] )  if
    :instrument
      $phase 4 >=  '( $n $p length extras timbres-of )
                   '( ( :fixedtimbres T@@ $phase 1 - @ ) )  if      // one timbre, or one stack of them, for every note
    zip ;

// ---- a phase, and the ascent -------------------------------------------------

// phase 1 .. 4: the levels of the ambitus 0, 0..1 ... 0..12, one after another
: phase-seq ( $phase -- seq )
  ( 0 :top $phase per-phase 1 + range  '( dup $phase swap attempts level-of ) map ** ) flatten ;

// a canon: the seq played by n voices, the second entering :delay units after the first, the
// third after the second ... Each is the same notes; they sound together.
: canon ( $seq $n $phase -- par )
  | 0 $n range
    '( :delay $phase per-phase  :unit $phase per-phase  * *  dup 0 >  '( $seq swap delay )  '( drop $seq )  if )  map ** par ;

// phase 1 .. 4 as the voices it has (:voices)
: phase-voices ( $phase -- music ) $phase phase-seq  :voices $phase per-phase  $phase canon ;

// the phases in the list, one after another: '[1 2 3 4] is the ascent; each prints its number
// while it is computed, which takes a moment
: phases-seq ( $phases -- seq ) ( $phases '( dup . phase-voices ) map ** ) flatten ;

// ---- start and stop ----------------------------------------------------------

: tempo-ctx ( $tempo -- ctx ) | :duration 1 :Tempo $tempo >ctx ;

// the phases of the list, in order: '[1] the mineral alone, '[1 2 3 4] all four
: start ( $phases -- ) stop  :seed T@ rng/seed  $phases phases-seq  :tempo T@ tempo-ctx  -> ;

: stop-ascent ( -- ) stop ;
